    {
      "filename": "AST-02-136 - Apollo Soyuz Test Project - Apollo Soyuz Test Project, Earth view, Egypt, Cairo, Nile River, Lake Oarum - NARA - 16627198.jpg",
      "title": "File:AST-02-136 - Apollo Soyuz Test Project - Apollo Soyuz Test Project, Earth view, Egypt, Cairo, Nile River, Lake Oarum - NARA - 16627198.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/AST-02-136_-_Apollo_Soyuz_Test_Project_-_Apollo_Soyuz_Test_Project%2C_Earth_view%2C_Egypt%2C_Cairo%2C_Nile_River%2C_Lake_Oarum_-_NARA_-_16627198.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AST-02-136_-_Apollo_Soyuz_Test_Project_-_Apollo_Soyuz_Test_Project,_Earth_view,_Egypt,_Cairo,_Nile_River,_Lake_Oarum_-_NARA_-_16627198.jpg",
      "width": 4400,
      "height": 4600,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Unknown authorUnknown author or not provided",
      "description": "Scope and content:  The original database describes this as:\nDescription: Apollo Soyuz Test Project (ASTP), Earth view, Egypt,Cairo,Nile River,Lake Oarum. Image taken on Revolution 71. Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) Time of Photo 201:00:41,Ground Elapsed Time (GET) 110:51,Altitude 221. Original Film Magazine: CX-12,Laboratory Roll 2; Camera Data: Hasselbald Reflex,70-mm,Model 500EL,NASA Modified; Film Data: 70-mm Ektachrome,MS,Type QX-807,ASA=64,250mm Lens.\nSubject Terms: Apollo Soyuz Test Project, Earth Observations (From Space), Africa, Egypt\nCategories: Earth Observations\nDate: 7/20/1975\nOriginal: Film - 70MM CT\nInterior_Exterior: Exterior\nGround_Orbit: On-orbit\nPart of this photo was used in Figure 2 of Utilization of ASTP Photographs in the Study of Small Structures in Abu Rawâsh and Wâdi el Natrûn, Egypt by Hassan A. El-Etr and Farouk El -Baz, in the Apollo-Soyuz Test Project Summary Science Report, Volume II, Earth Observations and Photography (1979, NASA SP-412), which has the following caption:\n\nFIGURE 2. - Orbital photograph detail of Abu Rawâsh.  (a) Part of ASTP photograph AST-02-136 showing the Abu Rawâsh area west of the Nile Delta. The dark green-gray color on the right edge represents vegetation and the shades of dark earthy gold are those of desert formations. Note the whitish color in the area of folded and faulted structures (1) and the dark-gray color of eroded basalt exposures (2). (b) Drawing of an enlargement of part of the area illustrated in figure 2 (a).  Within the light-toned area, dashed lines indicate structural elements, arrows give direction of plunge of folds, and solid lines indicate faults. Shaded areas are covered by debris from volcanic (basaltic) intrusions in the otherwise sedimentary surface.",
      "dateCreated": "between 15 July 1975 and 24 July 1975<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1975-07-00T00:00:00Z/10,P1319,+1975-07-15T00:00:00Z/11,P1326,+1975-07-24T00:00:00Z/11</div>",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "nile-wk",
      "sourceGeohash4": "sdz0",
      "mediumPath": "_m/s/d/z/0/nile-wk/ast-02-136-apollo-soyuz-test-p-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/s/d/z/0/nile-wk/ast-02-136-apollo-soyuz-test-p-small.webp"
    },
